# shellcheck shell=bash
# Invocation behind output/evaluation/anonymisation_single_meeting/
# (anonymisation_summary.json and anonymisation_report.csv): the
# single-meeting configuration, 200 AMI test utterances read from the front
# of the split with no per-meeting cap, which is the meeting EN2002a and its
# four speakers, at alphas 0.5, 0.7, 0.8 and 0.9. It is kept beside the
# multi-meeting result as the comparison with the August runs, which had
# this configuration.
#
# Job 8917988 (au_anon1), 2026-09-28, <project-a>, an NVIDIA L40S on
# htc-g078, at code 6f9bf56 with a clean tree, as its environment record and
# the summary's run_metadata say. It ran the single-meeting preset and wrote
# to ${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/audit2026/anon_single.
# Its speaker embeddings came from pyannote/wespeaker-voxceleb-resnet34-LM
# loaded directly, for the reason and with the equivalence check recorded in
# hpc/runs/anonymisation.env.
#
# It repeats the configuration of job 8573363 (2026-08-22, ANON_LIMIT=200 and
# these alphas, the result committed at 472ac19, whose files are still in
# ${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation on ARC) but not its
# sample. The August code took the first 200 usable rows in the order the
# dataset streams them. Since 7527331 the rows are grouped by meeting first,
# and evaluation.ami_meetings.group_rows_by_meeting sorts each meeting by
# start time, so this run took the first 200 usable utterances of EN2002a in
# start-time order. Only 36 utterances are in both samples, and the four
# speakers' shares moved from 58/51/49/42 to 86/47/38/29 (FEO072, MEE073,
# MEE071, FEO070). The summary's sampling field, "first usable utterances of
# the split, in stream order", is true of the meetings' order only. The
# first committed result, job 8556951 (2026-08-12, commit 0c4055d), had the
# same configuration as job 8573363 and drew the same 200 utterances in the
# same order.
#
# On the 36 shared utterances the original arm scores identically and
# self-similarity moves by at most 0.013. The change in the baseline
# therefore comes from the sample, and so, very largely, does the change in
# linkage, since the embeddings barely moved. The warped arm's word error
# rate is another matter. Between the August transform and the one at
# 6f9bf56 its errors differ on 15, 7, 5 and 4 of the 36 utterances at alpha
# 0.5, 0.7, 0.8 and 0.9, and the largest differences are decoder loops that
# appear or disappear: one utterance goes from 15 to 356 errors at alpha
# 0.5, another from 148 to 7 at alpha 0.7 and a third from 0 to 221 at
# alpha 0.9. The movement of the warped word error rate and of the cost
# therefore mixes the change of sample with the change to the transform.
#
# Reproduce (from the repository root on ARC), on the card type the original
# ran on:
#   ( set -a; . hpc/runs/anonymisation_single_meeting.env || exit 1; set +a
#     sbatch --account='<your-project>' --gres=gpu:l40s:1 hpc/submit_anonymisation.sh )
#
# REPORT_DIR below sends a reproduction to its own directory under repro/, so
# it cannot overwrite the original in audit2026/anon_single.
ANON_PRESET=single-meeting
REPORT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/repro/anonymisation_single_meeting"
